.Dd $Mdocdate: November 16 2026 $
.Dt IMAPIDLECTL 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm imapidlectl
.Nd show and set imapidle memory
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm imapidlectl
.Op Fl s Ar path
.Op Ar name ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
asks the running
.Sy imapidle(1)
for the values it holds in memory.
The default socket is
.Pa ~/var/run/imapidle.sock .
.Fl s
names another socket.
.Pp
With no
.Ar name ,
every node is printed as
.Ar name Ns = Ns Ar value .
A
.Ar name
prints that node and every node under it.
.Ar name Ns = Ns Ar value
sets a writable node and prints the result.
.Pp
A component that contains a dot is written with the dot doubled,
so a mailbox
.Ql INBOX.Sent
is
.Ql INBOX..Sent .
.Pp
.Ar shutdown=1
asks the daemon to exit the way
.Dv SIGTERM
does.
It does not create a shutdown file, so the next start is not held.
.Ar pause=1
pauses
.Sy mbsync
the way a pause file does.
.Ar pause=0
clears a pause that was set this way.
A pause file is left in place and still pauses.
.Ar account.name.folder.box.resync
sets how long that watched folder may go since its last sync.
The value is whole seconds, at least 60.
The default is 43200.
A dot inside the mailbox name is still doubled.
A reload reads the value from the configuration again.
.Ar account.name.hyperdelete
is 1 to sync a removal, or 0 to leave it until the next arrival
or that folder's resync time.
A reload reads this value from the configuration again.
.Ar account.name.next_try
is when that account logs in again, as seconds since the epoch.
Zero tries on the next loop.
Three authentication failures in a row set this one week ahead.
The write clears that hold.
.Ar account.name.disabled
is 0 or 1.
The write is remembered until the next start or reload.
The configuration file is not rewritten, and the file is applied
again at start and at reload.
.Ar disabled=1
drops that account's connections and does not set a future login.
.Ar disabled=0
clears the pause, the connect backoff, and a pending login hold,
including an authentication week.
.Ar limit.server.port.user.cap
is how many sessions this process may hold for that server,
port, and user.
The value is a whole number.
Zero is allowed.
.Ar limit.server.port.user.probe
is when one extra session may be tried, in seconds since
the epoch.
Zero tries on the next login.
A dot inside the server or the user is doubled.
Both values are kept in
.Pa ~/.local/imapidle/conn-limit
and a reload leaves them in place.
A write this process does not apply is an error.
.Pp
The reply is one node per line.
An unknown name or a rejected write is an error on standard error,
and
.Nm
exits 1.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa ~/var/run/imapidle.sock
The default socket.
Mode 0600.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std imapidlectl
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Sy imapidle(1) ,
.Sy imapidle.conf(5)
